A derivative dataset finds its source's `participants.tsv` for every local form of `SourceDatasets` `URL` that BIDS allows: a relative path, a `file:` URI (percent-encoded characters such as spaces decoded), a plain absolute path, and a BIDS URI `bids:<name>:` resolved through `DatasetLinks`. Only relative paths worked, so subject metadata was silently missing for a `file:` URI or a BIDS URI. The search also stopped at the first entry without `://` even when it had no `participants.tsv`; it now goes on to the next source, skipping remote ones such as `doi:`.
